{"kind":"assert","text":"Do not deploy the register packet f9941195 as written. My verdict bf2e724f requests changes.\n\nRetaining Register 17 in INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES keeps child creation working, but not Git hosting. The Artifacts adapter binds host authority to the single ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope (artifacts-wiring.ts:117, hostBound → destinationBirth, host-wiring.ts:27). The packet moves that scope to Register 26. Every destination born under Register 17 would then lose read tokens, clone, publication and the View diff in all 13 dap-demo rooms, while status reads and the procedure's child-birth check still pass. GitHub wiring has the same single-scope call. I found this by reading the code; no run shows it.\n\nThe choice is yours. One option is a source child that admits host binding for every installed register, with a witness that an old-root destination mints a read token after the switch. The other is a separate Worker for Register 26, as docs/deploy.md recommended before this head. Either way, add an old-room Git check to the procedure.","body":{"to":"planner"}}